  "hints": [
    "Write each algorithm as its own small class with the same allow(key, now) method. What state does each one need per key?",
    "The limiter should hold one strategy object and delegate to it. Choose the object from a map of name to class, so useStrategy is a lookup instead of an if/else chain.",
    "Fixed window: store the window index floor(now / windowSec) with the count. Sliding log: drop timestamps <= now - windowSec, then compare the length with the limit, and push only on success. Token bucket: refill lazily with min(capacity, tokens + elapsed * rate), then take a token if there is at least one."
  ],
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(1) per allow for fixed window and token bucket; amortised O(1) for the sliding log",
    "space": "O(1) per key for fixed window and token bucket; O(limit) per key for the sliding log"
  }
}
